            <ArticleTitle>[Nongynecologic abdominal emergencies during pregnancy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>269-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The paper reports on the authors' experience in the surgical emergency of a special category of patients: pregnant women with acute affections requiring surgery. The clinical aspects, sometimes deceptive, diagnosis difficulties and tactile and technical surgical attitudes are presented in detail.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
